// Title: HackTool - Pypykatz Credentials Dumping Activity
// Sigma ID: a29808fd-ef50-49ff-9c7a-59a9b040b404
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-05 | Modified: 2023-02-05
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.002
// Description: Detects the usage of "pypykatz" to obtain stored credentials. Adversaries may attempt to extract
//   credential material from the Security Account Manager (SAM) database through Windows registry
//   where the SAM database is stored
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/skelsec/pypykatz
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1003.002/T1003.002.md#atomic-test-2---registry-parse-with-pypykatz
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_pypykatz.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\pypykatz.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\python.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "live" and ProcessCommandLine contains "registry")
